  "id": "impulse-control",
  "term": "impulse control",
  "definition": "Impulse control refers to a person’s ability to hold back urges or rewarding behaviors that may become excessive or hard to resist. In this source, problems with impulse control appear as impulse control disorders such as gambling, hypersexuality, compulsive shopping, binge eating, hobbyism or punding, and dopamine dysregulation syndrome.",
